= Confronting Antisemitism

Since the Hamas attack of 7 October 2023, antisemitic incidents in Germany have reached record levels. They come from the far right, from Islamists and from parts of the left, and Jewish families ask whether they still have a future here. The AfD claims to protect Jews while its members play down the Holocaust.

- @socialism_of_fools: Antisemitism is the "socialism of fools". We will defeat it with social justice.
- @if: Antisemitism is a crisis. Launch a dedicated campaign against it.
- @all: Fight all forms of hatred together, without a separate campaign.

@socialism_of_fools

The best answer to hatred is economic security, so that fewer people look for scapegoats. We focus on our social programme.

@if
on-arrival: confronting_antisemitism += 2; democratization += 1; nationalism -= 3*(1-dissent); workers_afd -= 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_afd -= 2*(1-dissent); trust_in_democracy += 2

We fund Jewish community security and education projects in schools, and make clear in every local party that antisemitism has no place in the SPD, whoever it comes from. Hopefully our campaign can win people back from the far right.

@all

We campaign against racism, antisemitism and hostility to Muslims together, as one fight for human dignity.
